06. Recruitment Training Guide

Prompt V1
You are a student recruitment team leader. Review the product brief for the new Double Degree – Bachelor of Computer Science + Master of Data Science and create a one-page guide with key information about the course.

Prompt V2
You are a student engagement team leader. Review the product brief and create a quick-reference training guide for the Student Engagement Advisors to use in their conversations with students.

The guide should include:

Essential course information, including qualification, duration, delivery mode, entry requirements and areas of study
The five strongest course benefits, ranked in order of importance
Suggested discovery questions advisors can ask
Responses to potential FAQs – a maximum of 5 questions
A short “Why choose this course?” summary
A clearly labelled section showing information that is missing, unconfirmed or subject to university approval

Do not invent course details, fees, career outcomes, accreditation, scholarships, internships or industry commitments.

Do not make unsupported claims such as “unique”, “industry-leading” or “the only course of its kind”.

Distinguish between confirmed course facts and recommended advisor talking points.

Keep the final guide to approximately one printed page.
